  "notes": [
    "Sink instruction C+1 selects captured source C; registered sink changes C+2.",
    "VM RQ eight bank minor tuples {valid,sector16}; iteration*vmstep added to each sector; VM metadata 4x33 accompanies request.",
    "RGX and delivery address offsets add iteration*their respective steps; injection idx and low16 metadata bits add iteration*injidxstep; each40b injection address adds iteration*injaddrstep.",
    "Source metadata33 bits opaque flit header matching endpoint ABI; compiler must set real source/index/mode.",
    "Program is actual static lowered ISA; full normative record compiler/entry producer join remains required.",
    "vm_pair_select four6b entries {high_bank3,low_bank3}, explicit input sector assembly. Parent raw input capture then assembly output register adds2edges; registered VMrequest P gives qslots VMcapture P+10.",
    "Ring fields0..57 retain V1 semantics. Ring bits58..81 are ARhigh,82 capture_arg,83 reduce_clear;84..87 remain reserved zero.",
    "Each logical sequence16 is {high10,low6}+iteration*iter_link_slot_step. Overflow>=65536 faults; physicalslotseq[5:0] reuses64SRAMslots afterreadconsume; no normalepochdrain.",
    "SWcapturemask={capture_arg,capture_slot10}; q2capturemask=capture_slot10 andARGsource9mustremain0. Selectorwidth4 staysfixed.",
    "Reduce input from last qslots sink; compiled load_v/add_read validates actual incomingflit. Read/addissue and pubread/pubissue are one edge apart.",
    "ARGmode statically routes four formerTKMsinks toARG; TKMvalid andslot0 inARGmode. ARGout independent qslots source, no reduction/ARG outputdata mux.",
    "V1 596 source remains frozen for existing native proof; V2 operation/program/physical qualification remains separate.",
    "V2 endpoint sequence metadata is registered: emit all wr/rd/rx full-sequence fields one edge before the corresponding reservation bits; extended overflow is retained with metadata and faults on consumption.",
    "V3 native pinregistered endpoint: rd reservation C ->registered physical TX C+5, RX captureR ->registered payloadR+1. Compiler advances rd by2 edges relative to V2 for a fixed physical launch; wr/data occupancy must preserve native64-slot lifetime. Actual issuer busy/fault/uop_v/uop_pc feedback is exposed to host assembler."
  ],
